<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lunda Empire</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Lunda Kingdom, Lunda</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Lunda Empire was a Central African state in the south of the present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/democratic-republic-of-the-congo">Democratic Republic of the Congo</a> and parts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/angola">Angola</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zambia">Zambia</a>, flourishing from the seventeenth to the nineteenth century. Its kingship drew on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luba-empire">Luba</a> political models, and it expanded through a flexible system of tributary chiefdoms. It traded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-trade">ivory</a> and slaves across the region and took part in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-slave-trade">Atlantic trade</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lunda-empire.jpg" alt="Lunda Empire" width="320" height="394" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Library of Congress · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lunda_Empire.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
